dia/thumbs/caedmon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cædmon</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Cædmon was a cowherd at the monastery of Whitby under Abbess Hild who, according to Bede, received the gift of composing religious verse in a dream.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/caedwalla"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/caedwalla.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cædwalla</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Cædwalla was king of Wessex from about 685 to 688.</span></a></li></ul>
